Third-party data: SunSpec model definitions
-------------------------------------------

models.json is a derived subset of the SunSpec information model
definitions published by the SunSpec Alliance:

  Source:     https://github.com/sunspec/models, directory json/, files
              model_<id>.json
  Version:    commit 90b4a331dcca1d6eac69c1bead952fddcc5852e0 (master,
              2026-08-20, the merge of pull request #278; after the tag
              v2026-04-20)
  Licence:    Apache License, Version 2.0 (the repository's LICENSE)
  Copyright:  the SunSpec Alliance, which publishes the repository. The
              repository itself states no copyright line: at that commit
              its LICENSE is the Apache-2.0 text with the appendix
              template ("Copyright [yyyy] [name of copyright owner]") not
              filled in, it has no NOTICE file, and neither its README nor
              the model files carry a copyright statement (checked on
              2026-10-11). The SunSpec Alliance's own Python library,
              pysunspec2, marks its files "Copyright (C) 2020 SunSpec
              Alliance".

What was taken (since v0.2.0 for every one of the 112 models at that
commit, 1 to 19, 101 to 145, 160, 201 to 220, 302 to 308, 401 to 404,
501, 502, 601, 701 to 715, 801 to 809, 63001, 63002 and 64001 to 64415;
v0.1.0 had 25 of them): each point's name, offset, type, size, scale
factor, unit, access, mandatory and static flags, symbol names and
values, and short label; the groups' names, places, lengths, counts and
nesting; each model's name and short label. Descriptions, comments and
other prose of the definitions were not taken. The data was reshaped
into this module's own JSON layout (short keys, offsets counted from the
first register after ID and L) by internal/modelgen, whose output at that
commit is the file as shipped. The interop tests compare all 3578 points
with pysunspec2 1.3.6's copy of the definitions (equal, apart from the
modification below).

The vendor models in the definitions (64001 to 64415) carry names of
their makers' products in their own names and labels; the module's short
names for them do not.

Modifications: the symbol names of model 111's St point are written
OFF ... STANDBY, as in models 101 to 113; the source prefixes them with
"gg". Leading and trailing spaces of labels are dropped. The file states
its origin and these changes in its "source" field.

